claim.claim-text:
1. A method comprising:
receiving a plurality of primitives that define visual changes that occur to dynamic three-dimensional (3D) content across a plurality of frames;
determining a first set of primitives from the plurality of primitives that remain unchanged for at least N frames of the plurality of frames and a second set of primitives from the plurality of primitives that remain unchanged for less than the N frames, wherein N is a value greater than 1;
generating a first data stream that encodes the first set of primitives at a reduced frame rate that is less than a desired frame rate, wherein the first data stream encodes the first set of primitives with temporal values that specify which two or more frames of the plurality of frames at which to present different primitives of the first set of primitives;
generating a second data stream that encodes the second set of primitives without temporal values at the desired frame rate and with each different frame at the desired frame rate encoding data of one or more primitives from the second set of primitives that are presented without change at that different frame;
receiving a request for the 3D content; and
streaming the first data stream and the second data stream in response to the request.

16. A streaming system comprising:
one or more hardware processors configured to:
receive a plurality of primitives that define visual changes that occur to dynamic three-dimensional (3D) content across a plurality of frames;
determine a first set of primitives from the plurality of primitives that remain unchanged for at least N frames of the plurality of frames and a second set of primitives from the plurality of primitives that remain unchanged for less than the N frames, wherein N is a value greater than 1;
generate a first data stream that encodes the first set of primitives at a reduced frame rate that is less than a desired frame rate, wherein the first data stream encodes the first set of primitives with temporal values that specify which two or more frames of the plurality of frames at which to present different primitives of the first set of primitives;
generate a second data stream that encodes the second set of primitives without temporal values at the desired frame rate and with each different frame at the desired frame rate encoding data of one or more primitives from the second set of primitives that are presented without change at that different frame;
receive a request for the 3D content; and
stream the first data stream and the second data stream in response to the request.

20. A non-transitory computer-readable medium storing instructions that, when executed by one or more processors of a streaming system, cause the streaming system to perform operations comprising:
receiving a plurality of primitives that define visual changes that occur to dynamic three-dimensional (3D) content across a plurality of frames;
determining a first set of primitives from the plurality of primitives that remain unchanged for at least N frames of the plurality of frames and a second set of primitives from the plurality of primitives that remain unchanged for less than the N frames, wherein N is a value greater than 1;
generating a first data stream that encodes the first set of primitives at a reduced frame rate that is less than a desired frame rate, wherein the first data stream encodes the first set of primitives with temporal values that specify which two or more frames of the plurality of frames at which to present different primitives of the first set of primitives;
generating a second data stream that encodes the second set of primitives without temporal values at the desired frame rate and with each different frame at the desired frame rate encoding data of one or more primitives from the second set of primitives that are presented without change at that different frame;
receiving a request for the 3D content; and
streaming the first data stream and the second data stream in response to the request.
